title:: BMAutoBalancerGUI
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - a GUI for BMAutoBalancer
categories:: Classes

Description::

This class provides a GUI for the utility class methods found in link::Classes/Other/BMAutoBalancer::. Hardware input channels start from 1 in the GUI, not 0.

See also: link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractGUI::, link::Classes/Other/BMAutoBalancer::

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
Create a new BMAutoBalancerGUI.

argument:: speakerList
The link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray:: to balance. This is done in place.
argument:: okayFunc
An optional link::Classes/Function:: to evaluate when the cycle is complete. This will be passed strong::speakerList:: as an argument.
argument:: server
The link::Classes/Server:: to use. nil indicates the default server.
argument:: name
An optional link::Classes/String:: or link::Classes/Symbol:: indicating the title of the window. Default is "Autobalance Speakers".
argument:: origin
An optional link::Classes/Point:: specifying the origin of the window. Default is 400@600.


Examples::

code::
l = [BMSpeaker(\left, 0), BMSpeaker(\right, 1), BMSpeaker(\sub, 2, spec: 'Generic Sub')].as(BMInOutArray); // sub will be ignored

BMAutoBalancerGUI(l); 
::
